# .riv intentionally NOT routed through Git LFS.
# Netlify's deploy pipeline only hydrates LFS content for known media
# extensions (mp4/mov/webm). .riv is a Rive-specific binary format
# Netlify doesn't recognize, so LFS pointers were being served to
# production verbatim (content-length 132, starting with "version
# https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1"), which broke the Rive runtime
# with "Bad header / Problem loading file; may be corrupt!"
# Committing .riv as regular git binaries. All 4 current files are
# under 7MB each (under the 10MB pre-commit guard). See WORKLOG entry
# for 2026-04-20.
*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mov filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webm filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
